The underlying Tang poems are ancient works. The project consults scans whose
Wikimedia Commons file pages mark them as public-domain scans; it does not
claim copyright in the source texts and does not redistribute the scan files.
Public-domain status can vary by jurisdiction, so users should verify the
linked file-page notices for their own use:

- 1933 edition of 唐詩三百首, used as the base witness for 49 poems,
  National Library of China scan on Wikimedia Commons:
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NLC416-17jh000616-101322_%E5%94%90%E8%A9%A9%E4%B8%89%E7%99%BE%E9%A6%96.pdf
- 1933 edition of 本事詩, used only as the base witness for
  題都城南莊 because the specified 1933 唐詩三百首 does not include it;
  National Library of China scan on Wikimedia Commons:
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NLC511-027032013010163-20835_%E6%9C%AC%E4%BA%8B%E8%A9%A9.pdf
- 1705 御定全唐詩 scans on Wikimedia Commons:
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:%E5%BE%A1%E5%AE%9A%E5%85%A8%E5%94%90%E8%A9%A9

Each poem in this small, independently reviewed selection uses two witnesses
drawn from the three scanned bibliographic editions listed above. It is not
presented as an authoritative scholarly critical edition.
